lines+=['## Source anomalies and repairs','q-168615 and q-168624 contain the response line and matching field-1 placeholder but omit the vector declaration. Their worked-solution formal operator rows identify respectively F=⟨z²,2xy,xy²⟩ and G=⟨0,0,-xy-2z²⟩. The public source_* recipes preserve raw prompt strings and are evidence_only, eligible_for_learning=false. Public easy templates zero_terms and axial prepend those complete declarations with parameterized scale, retain the original blank shape and solution sequence, and are supported_presentation_repair, eligible_for_learning=true. These are two supported prompt repairs, separate from exact raw replay counts.','q-123179 begins its explanation with F=P+Qj+Rk: the i after P is missing. This prose typo remains in raw evidence. Normal shared_square output uses the common correct P i+Q j+R k opening. It is one prose repair, separate from the two incomplete prompt repairs; no mathematical value or source correct designation needs repair.','All 14 source difficulty labels and correct references are present. No missing-label inference or missing-correct designation is counted as a match. The local original MA lesson 2131 Source/2131.json confirms the 3D lesson narrative and canonical example but does not contain the later q-168615/q-168624 widgets; component repair therefore relies on captured ordered derivative inputs and independent mathematical checking, not a claim that an unavailable widget was inspected.']
