lines+=['## 4. Reusable templates, constraints and authored extension','Fixed: every original teaching sentence, ordered equality-row sequence, operators, coordinate identities, response shape, source point, and baseline complete observed bank. Variable: complete component scale c. Conditional: multiplication by unity is omitted; a negative coefficient is grouped; a negative displayed component whose original sign supplied the separator receives an explicit separator when scaled. Mask construction operates on complete component spans before replacement, so a basis label, function argument or coordinate tuple is never changed by a short global substring replacement.','Normal authored templates use a,b,c in {-3,-2,-1,1,2,3}, enforced on explicit calls and sampling. Symbolic components and derivative expressions are canonicalized, dropping additive terms constant in their differentiated coordinate. Bank/profile, answer layout, seed and option order do not enter the mathematical fingerprint. Moderate point aliases merge when actual canonical fields, derivative tasks and independently evaluated derivative contribution tuples agree. Different fields that merely share a final scalar remain distinct tasks. Full content identity contains version, displayed prompt, complete fixed solution, type, difficulty and complete bank values.','Authored easy exp_sine differentiates exp(ax) with a held yz trig factor, xyz, and a constant; monomial differentiates three simple monomial/exp components; shared_square applies three linear chain factors before collection and rejects a+b+c=0. These preserve the observed easy families and two/three substantive derivative contributions.','Authored moderate evaluated_monomial, evaluated_square and evaluated_exp_trig perform the same three coordinate derivatives then small exact substitution. Point coordinates are integers with magnitude <=2. Monomial coordinates and square arguments must be nonzero. Exponential/trig evaluation has y=0 and nonzero x,z, keeping e^0 and cos(0) familiar. No arbitrary transcendental numerical evaluation is added.','Authored hard product_exp and product_log each require six substantive derivative summands: a two-term product/chain derivative for each of P,Q,R. Powers are at most two; integer coefficient magnitudes <=3; hard is symbolic to avoid unrelated arithmetic difficulty. product_log restricts 2+xz>0. Both families demand equal workload and have no internal progression. Their use of product and chain rules is grounded in observed easy shared affine squares, observed moderate y sin(pi y) product/chain differentiation, the canonical 3D example, and prerequisite Partial Differentiability of Multivariable Functions. Hard is a supported design claim, not an observed source label.','Ordered lesson route (followed via activity/first-step and step/next, never collection order): '+ ' → '.join(r['title'] for r in route)+'. The preceding Visualizing Vector Fields and Partial Differentiability topics establish the objects and held-coordinate derivatives. The later Properties of the Divergence Operator and Green’s Theorem are excluded: there are no flux integrals, curl, theorem applications or conceptual sink/source tasks in these generators.','Authored radio bank is selected before parameters. With three nonzero derivatives Dp,Dq,Dr, it contains D, D-Dp, D-Dq, D-Dr, -D. The two-derivative constant-component family contains D, Dp, Dq, -Dp+Dq, D+R. At a point, each complete expression is evaluated there. Any equality, correct distractor, zero-divergence negation collision or missing member rejects the whole parameter tuple; no first-valid pool is used. Authored blank has one verified expression and no distractor bank. Raw observed banks never silently replace these operations.','Plot extraction/specification: none. No source prompt, answer, or solution for this KP contains a plot or image. The neighboring interpretation KP’s diagrams do not belong to this KP and are not imported.']
(HERE/'template-extraction.md').write_text('\n\n'.join(lines)+'\n')
(HERE/'README.md').write_text('''# Three-dimensional divergence generator

Run `.venv/bin/python generate/scratch/17592186133889/validate.py`.
Preview `.venv/bin/python generate/scratch/17592186133889.py --difficulty all --seed 7 --count 2 --format markdown`.

The script exposes generate_easy, generate_moderate, generate_hard and generate(level, seed=0, template=None, field_type=None, parameters=None, profile=None). Normal radio/blank templates are in TEMPLATES. Supported easy blank repairs zero_terms and axial accept parameters={"scale":c}. Public evidence replay uses template="source_q-105555", parameters={"scale":1}, profile="observed_q-105555" (and similarly all source IDs in source-cases.json). Evidence profiles are explicitly ineligible for learning. Scale is a complete-component mathematical parameter; authored a,b,c families provide wider meaningful practice.

Validation separately checks all raw prompts, complete prose/row sequence, field layouts and key presence, all complete bank values and designations; parses actual displayed components, formal operator inputs, individual authored held-coordinate contributions, every reduction/evaluation row and complete banks; checks deterministic identity, reduced workload guards, finite task catalogs and real native engine grading. Two incomplete source blank prompts and one prose typo are documented separately from exact replay. Hard scope is authored and has no observed source labels. No plots are needed. No EDB writes, registration or engine edits occur.

Read classification.md, template-extraction.md, validation.json and review.md for evidence and bounds. Source provenance is the math basis-1356 wrapper in source.json. frozen-shas.json freezes artifacts and captured source/context/engine provenance for parent QA; its own hash is excluded.
''')
